You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S07
Scenario title: Meeting Summary and Email Reporting
Initial workflow description:
After a meeting, the contents are summarized and shared by email with the relevant people.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What event or action officially signals that a meeting has ended and that the summarization process should begin?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "How is the meeting summary currently created — for example, is it written manually by a participant, produced by a dedicated note-taker, or generated using a transcription or AI tool?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "What specific sections or elements are required in a meeting summary, such as decisions made, action items with owners, agenda topics covered, or attendee list?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "How are the recipients of the summary email determined — is it automatically taken from the meeting attendee list, a predefined group, or manually selected each time?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "Before the summary email is sent, does anyone need to review or approve the content, and if so, who holds that responsibility?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "Is there a defined time limit within which the summary email must be sent after the meeting concludes, and what happens if that deadline is missed?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
